# Catch up

1. **Git.** `git fetch --prune`, `git status -sb`. On a clean `main` behind `origin/main`, `git pull --ff-only`.
   List local branches not merged (`git branch --no-merged main`).
2. **GitHub.** `gh pr list` and `gh issue list --limit 10`.
3. **Dependencies.** `uv sync`.
4. **Data.** `uv run {{ project_name }} status`. Say how fresh the data is, and any contract problem.
{%- if motherduck %}
5. **Published copy.** `uv run {{ project_name }} publish --check`. If it is stale, say so (do not publish: only on request).
{%- endif %}
{%- if cloud_run %}
6. **Hosted app.** The deployed commit (`gcloud run services describe {{ project_name }} --project={{ gcp_project }} --region={{ gcp_region }} --format="value(spec.template.metadata.labels.commit)"`) against `origin/main` (`git rev-list --count <commit>..origin/main`).
{%- endif %}
7. **The app.** Health of http://localhost:{{ app_port }}: running or not.
8. **Scaffold.** `uv run {{ project_name }} doctor --remote`. If a newer release is out, suggest `/scaffold-update`.

Report in a short list: what changed, what needs attention, and a suggested next step. Change nothing beyond the
pull and `uv sync`.
